   All known proper partial geometries Π with an abelian Singer group G which are different
from the Van Lint-Schrijver geometry have the following properties.

   • G is elementary abelian.

   • Π is of spread type.

The main thrust of this paper is to investigate whether these two properties must hold for all
partial geometries with abelian Singer groups different from the Van Lint-Schrijver geometry.
   Some interesting results on this problem are known already: the order of an abelian
