1.2   Maximum Cut
Given a graph G, a cut in G is a partition (U, V ) of the vertex set together with all the edges having
exactly one endpoint in both parts. The size of the cut is the number of its edges. The MaxCut of G
is the maximum size of a cut, denoted by mc(G). The MaxCut is among one the most studied graph
parameters, lying at the intersection of theoretical computer science [32, 40, 51], extremal combinatorics
[2, 3, 30, 35] and probabilistic graph theory [23, 22, 27]. In theoretical computer science, one is usually
